# =====================================================================================
# Passenger web subview (C117) — passenger.mageride.lk
#
# Every value here is read on the SERVER, and there is no `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable —
# nor may one be added. The share token is already in the visitor's address bar, so this
# is not about hiding a credential: it is about keeping the *platform* out of the
# browser. A page opened from an SMS on a stranger's phone talks to
# `passenger.mageride.lk` and to nothing else — one origin, one TLS handshake, no
# gateway address in any shipped script, and no CORS policy to widen on a no-login
# endpoint.
#
# Read at runtime, not inlined at build: the subview ships as one image
# (`output: 'standalone'`) and the same image runs on the lightweight replica and on
# DOKS with different values.
# =====================================================================================

# The C008 API gateway origin. `/public/{**remainder}` reaches public-bff, which is the
# only service this surface has (`backend/src/ApiGateway/gateway-routes.json`).
# REQUIRED. Absent, every page answers 503 and says the platform cannot be reached.
MAGERIDE_API_BASE_URL=http://api-gateway:8080

# --- The map (SCR-WT-002 / 003 / 004) ------------------------------------------------
#
# The MapLibre style document the three map screens draw their basemap from — D-14's
# `tile-cdn`: the Cloudflare R2 PMTiles bucket behind the Worker that serves range-byte
# requests (ADD §6, §10.2). A `pmtiles://` source in the style is understood; the
# protocol handler is registered by the map component.
#
# This is the ONE URL a browser fetches, and it is deliberately not the platform: tiles
# are static cartography, carry nobody's ride and take no credential. It is handed to the
# component as a prop, NOT published as NEXT_PUBLIC_* — the browser still never learns
# where the gateway is.
#
# OPTIONAL. Unset, the driver marker, the pins and the route render on an empty canvas
# and the screen says so: the marker is the data the screen exists for, and a missing
# basemap must not read as a missing driver.
WEB_PASSENGER_MAP_STYLE_URL=

# --- The app-download links (SCR-WT-002 / 005 / 006) ---------------------------------
#
# Where "Open MageRide" and the two "Get the app" strips point. Two variables because the
# two stores are two URLs and the visitor is on one of the two phones; the `User-Agent`
# picks, and either falls back to whichever one is set.
#
# BOTH OPTIONAL. With neither, the control is not drawn at all rather than drawn and
# dead — a control nobody can tell is broken is worse than no control. SCR-WT-006 is
# still a complete page without it: its copy already tells the reader to ask the sender
# for a new link.
WEB_PASSENGER_ANDROID_APP_URL=
WEB_PASSENGER_IOS_APP_URL=
